1
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:20,932
Ow! Oh!

2
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:23,977
Stop, stop, stop.

3
00:02:25,771 --> 00:02:27,647
Stop. Stop.

4
00:02:27,648 --> 00:02:29,774
No, Krypto. Krypto.

5
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:31,776
Ow!

6
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:36,739
Krypto.

7
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:39,534
Take me home.

8
00:02:43,664 --> 00:02:44,665
Home.

9
00:02:57,469 --> 00:02:58,470
Krypto.

10
00:02:59,221 --> 00:03:00,806
Home.

11
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:45,225
Superman!

12
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:01,866
Thank you.

13
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:05,286
No need to thank us, sir,
as we will not appreciate it.

14
00:04:05,287 --> 00:04:07,580
We have no consciousness whatsoever.

15
00:04:07,581 --> 00:04:10,583
Merely automatons, here to serve.

16
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:13,170
Meet Twelve. She's new.

17
00:04:13,963 --> 00:04:16,965
- Hi.
- He looked at me.

18
00:04:16,966 --> 00:04:19,884
I put your parents'
message on to soothe you.

19
00:04:19,885 --> 00:04:20,844
Thank you.

20
00:04:21,136 --> 00:04:23,012
He finds it soothing.

21
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:46,995
The message was damaged in transit
from Krypton to Earth.

22
00:04:46,996 --> 00:04:48,287
But what is there...

23
00:04:50,249 --> 00:04:52,458
"We love you
more than heaven, our son."

24
00:04:53,544 --> 00:04:56,421
"We love you more than land."

25
00:04:56,422 --> 00:04:59,132
"Our beloved home
will soon be gone forever.

26
00:04:59,133 --> 00:05:01,426
But hope vitalizes our hearts,

27
00:05:01,427 --> 00:05:03,637
and that hope is you, Kal-El."

28
00:05:05,389 --> 00:05:07,557
"We have searched
the universe for a home

29
00:05:07,558 --> 00:05:09,727
where you can do the most good

30
00:05:10,269 --> 00:05:12,521
and live out Krypton's truth.

31
00:05:13,605 --> 00:05:15,566
- That place is Earth."
- "That place is Earth."

32
00:05:16,275 --> 00:05:18,234
And the rest of the message is lost.

33
00:05:18,235 --> 00:05:19,944
Fourteen fractured bones.

34
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:23,449
Damage to bladder, kidney,
large intestine, lungs.

35
00:05:24,074 --> 00:05:25,867
Our poor Superman.

36
00:05:25,868 --> 00:05:27,827
With a healthy dose of yellow sun,

37
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:30,163
we'll have him up and at 'em in no time.

38
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:56,105
Engineer, come in.

39
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:58,274
He landed somewhere near here.

40
00:05:58,275 --> 00:05:59,610
I can't see where.

41
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,736
Well, keep looking.

42
00:06:09,536 --> 00:06:12,081
Golly.

43
00:06:14,208 --> 00:06:18,087
Sir, you are only 83% restored
to health. You must rest.

44
00:06:18,212 --> 00:06:20,339
No can do, Four.
I gotta get back to the fray.

45
00:06:20,756 --> 00:06:23,966
But this Hammer fellow
just beat you at full power.

46
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,219
Sir?

47
00:06:27,554 --> 00:06:29,138
What is this?

48
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,307
Krypto!

49
00:06:33,352 --> 00:06:34,936
What the hey, dude? I-I thought--

50
00:06:34,937 --> 00:06:36,230
You destroyed the whole--

51
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,940
Superman robots, I thought I told you
to keep an eye on him.

52
00:06:38,941 --> 00:06:41,150
We feed the canine, but he is unruly.

53
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:43,569
And he realizes
we are not flesh and blood

54
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:47,116
and couldn't, in our heart of hearts,
care less whether he lives or dies.

55
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:49,576
Stop, Krypto, leave it.

56
00:06:50,202 --> 00:06:52,745
Ow. Ow! Stop. Ow. Stop it.

57
00:06:52,746 --> 00:06:55,039
Krypto! Ow! Ow! Stop it. Stop.

58
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,126
Sit. Sit. Stay.

59
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:15,434
The alien is on its way back.

60
00:07:47,134 --> 00:07:49,845
Your Superman has abandoned you!

61
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:55,601
The people of Boravia will not ignore him
inserting himself into our affairs.

62
00:08:00,314 --> 00:08:02,857
Accelerate the portals.

63
00:08:02,858 --> 00:08:04,400
Primed and ready.

64
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:06,485
T-Minus ten and counting.

65
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:07,696
Buckle up, we're going live.

66
00:08:07,821 --> 00:08:09,780
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six...

67
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:11,282
Bravo, what do you have on employees?

68
00:08:11,283 --> 00:08:12,450
I'm inside Chocos, Larry. No fatalities.

69
00:08:12,451 --> 00:08:13,492
...five, four...

70
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:16,747
- Can't win 'em all.
- ...three, two, one.

71
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:20,333
Target in sight.

72
00:08:20,334 --> 00:08:23,378
- He's back. Your 5:00.
- Copy.

73
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:29,718
12C.

74
00:08:35,974 --> 00:08:36,850
18A.

75
00:08:42,189 --> 00:08:43,106
34B.

76
00:08:47,236 --> 00:08:48,111
98Z.

77
00:08:50,405 --> 00:08:51,073
8H.

78
00:08:54,284 --> 00:08:55,494
74D.

79
00:08:59,748 --> 00:09:01,041
44T!

80
00:09:11,635 --> 00:09:14,595
- Reggie, can you watch?
- Yeah, yeah.

81
00:09:17,057 --> 00:09:19,476
Yes! Yes, yes, yes!

82
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:24,021
It's like he knows Superman's every move
before he makes it.

83
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:26,899
He does. He's been studying him for years.

84
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:30,152
He's developed over 2,500 fight moves
for any situation.

85
00:09:30,153 --> 00:09:32,322
Superman!

86
00:09:33,699 --> 00:09:35,200
Bravo, you got him?

87
00:09:36,952 --> 00:09:39,079
Malik Ali, a local.

88
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,748
Lex, we have the Engineer.

89
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:45,377
The target
has led us to the ice castle.

90
00:09:46,044 --> 00:09:47,378
The rumors are true.

91
00:09:47,379 --> 00:09:49,923
I don't know how in the hell
this thing hasn't been spotted.

92
00:09:56,638 --> 00:09:57,639
Mierda.

93
00:10:04,521 --> 00:10:05,856
Comms, two to one.

94
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:09,401
Hijo de...

95
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:13,155
Lex, the entire structure
has descended into the ice.

96
00:10:13,989 --> 00:10:15,656
We have what we need.
Return to base.

97
00:10:15,657 --> 00:10:17,450
I can drill into it, Lex.

98
00:10:17,451 --> 00:10:19,493
Your pride won't be making
our choices today, Angela.

99
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:20,411
Thank you.

100
00:10:20,412 --> 00:10:22,122
We'll need more than you
when we enter.

101
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:25,250
Comms, one to two.

102
00:10:26,168 --> 00:10:28,170
We've done what we need to do.
Wrap it up.

103
00:10:28,712 --> 00:10:34,092
The United States will continue to feel
the wrath of the Hammer of Boravia.

104
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:35,719
It's me, Mali.

105
00:10:36,345 --> 00:10:37,804
Once I gave you free falafel,

106
00:10:38,305 --> 00:10:40,348
when you saved a woman
from being hit by a taxi.

107
00:10:40,349 --> 00:10:41,515
Are you all right, Superman?

108
00:10:41,516 --> 00:10:43,726
Mali, you gotta get outta here.
It's not safe.

109
00:10:43,727 --> 00:10:46,395
You saved us so many times.
Now it's our turn.

110
00:10:46,396 --> 00:10:48,523
This is your last warning.

111
00:10:49,232 --> 00:10:50,984
Oh!

112
00:10:54,237 --> 00:10:57,032
Maybe you shouldn't have done
that thing in Jarhanpur, Superman.

113
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:05,164
Flawless, people.

114
00:11:05,165 --> 00:11:06,875
Way to bring it home!

115
00:12:00,387 --> 00:12:02,222
Decelerate all portals.

116
00:12:04,266 --> 00:12:05,724
- Ultraman's back.
- Ultraman!

117
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:08,310
Ultraman! You did so good.

118
00:12:08,311 --> 00:12:09,770
Yes!

119
00:12:36,173 --> 00:12:37,466
Sorry about that. I'm so sorry.

120
00:12:38,675 --> 00:12:39,593
Sorry.

121
00:12:41,136 --> 00:12:42,637
- Morning, Nino.
- Good morning, Clark.

122
00:12:49,144 --> 00:12:51,270
Do these unelected metahumans

123
00:12:51,271 --> 00:12:53,939
think they can dictate
international policy?

124
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,191
It's outrageous.

125
00:12:55,192 --> 00:12:57,776
It's a big story.
Put it above the fold.

126
00:12:57,777 --> 00:12:59,403
That's where we put it.

127
00:12:59,404 --> 00:13:01,948
- You're late again, Kent.
- Sorry, Perry.

128
00:13:02,616 --> 00:13:05,035
- Hey, loser.
- Hey, Steve.

129
00:13:05,494 --> 00:13:07,870
Hey, what do you got
against adverbs, Kent?

130
00:13:07,871 --> 00:13:11,124
How are we supposed to know how we feel
when we read this malarkey?

131
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:15,462
In sports writing, you learn
the sentence is the modifier.

132
00:13:16,046 --> 00:13:17,464
- Hey, Ma.
- "Ma!"

133
00:13:18,006 --> 00:13:19,965
Hey, Clark!

134
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:22,718
Uh, me and Pa just wanted to call

135
00:13:22,719 --> 00:13:26,305
and say congratulations
on that front page.

136
00:13:26,306 --> 00:13:28,307
Boy, that is something!

137
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,809
Hey, ask Ma if she barbecued up
any good roadkill lately.

138
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:33,354
- Shut up, Steve.
- Like, uh, possum or chitlins...

139
00:13:33,355 --> 00:13:34,939
- What's that, Clark?
- Sorry, Ma,

140
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:36,065
I'm just in the middle
of a big news day here.

141
00:13:36,066 --> 00:13:37,149
What are chitlins?

142
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:38,692
Chitlins are intestines.

143
00:13:38,693 --> 00:13:40,987
Thanks, Cat. You read this crud?

144
00:13:41,363 --> 00:13:42,864
I thought it was great, Clark.

145
00:13:43,698 --> 00:13:44,740
"Great"?

146
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:46,951
Yeah! Front page! Big time!

147
00:13:46,952 --> 00:13:50,829
Well, we don't want
to keep you, but, uh,

148
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:53,041
wanted to say congrats,

149
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,835
and tell you we're thinking
'bout you, Clark.

150
00:13:55,961 --> 00:13:59,213
- It's been a minute.
- Tell him don't be a stranger.

151
00:13:59,214 --> 00:14:01,590
Pa says, "Don't be a stranger."

152
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:03,592
I, uh... Yeah, I heard him, Ma.

153
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:05,303
Yeah, okay I gotta go. I gotta run.

154
00:14:05,804 --> 00:14:06,637
Yep, okay. Love you.

155
00:14:06,638 --> 00:14:10,266
So, this guy just flew into midtown
and started attacking people,

156
00:14:10,267 --> 00:14:12,101
demanding for Superman to show up?

157
00:14:12,102 --> 00:14:14,144
Yeah. It's all there in my article.

158
00:14:14,145 --> 00:14:16,105
Then I'd actually have to make
it through your writing, Clark.

159
00:14:16,106 --> 00:14:18,315
Knowledge is worth many sacrifices.

160
00:14:18,316 --> 00:14:19,191
That isn't one of them.

161
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:21,068
Ha, ha, ha. Very funny, Lois.

162
00:14:21,069 --> 00:14:23,028
- Oh, my God.
- He's so fine.

163
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:26,073
Twenty-two people in the hospital,
over 20 million in property damage.

164
00:14:26,074 --> 00:14:28,076
- It does make you wonder.
- Wonder what?

165
00:14:28,201 --> 00:14:31,203
As great as he is, maybe Superman
didn't completely think through

166
00:14:31,204 --> 00:14:32,830
the ramifications of the Boravia thing.

167
00:14:32,831 --> 00:14:35,082
If this guy is even from Boravia.

168
00:14:35,083 --> 00:14:37,294
What do you mean?
His name is "the Hammer of Boravia."

169
00:14:37,419 --> 00:14:39,753
Yeah, I doubt his parents
named him that, Jimmy.

170
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:41,922
We have no clue
what his actual goal was here.

171
00:14:41,923 --> 00:14:44,383
I think it's pretty obvious the
goal was kicking Superman's ass.

172
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:46,427
Uh, he did-- He didn't
completely kick Superman's ass.

173
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:47,469
Pretty thoroughly, Clark.

174
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:51,348
Show me! You show me
what ties there are

175
00:14:51,349 --> 00:14:54,435
between Boravia and this "Hammer!"

176
00:14:54,436 --> 00:14:56,770
Yeah, see, Superman did say
he thought the, uh, Hammer

177
00:14:56,771 --> 00:14:58,356
might be faking a Boravian accent.

178
00:14:58,815 --> 00:14:59,815
Superman said that?

179
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:01,901
Yeah, I interviewed him
right afterwards. Great guy.

180
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:06,071
You know, it's funny that you keep getting
all these interviews with Superman, Clark.

181
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:08,867
I don't think there's anything funny
about good journalism, Lois.

182
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:10,284
Uh-huh.

183
00:15:10,285 --> 00:15:15,414
The relationship
between Boravia and United States

184
00:15:15,415 --> 00:15:19,419
has been like iron for 30 years,

185
00:15:19,794 --> 00:15:22,964
until Superman came along.

186
00:15:25,425 --> 00:15:27,051
What you're looking at,
my friends,

187
00:15:27,052 --> 00:15:30,805
is the most powerful being
on Planet Earth:

188
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:33,183
Ultraman.

189
00:15:33,808 --> 00:15:35,184
You created this man?

190
00:15:35,185 --> 00:15:38,354
Ooh. Check this out. The Engineer.

191
00:15:38,355 --> 00:15:40,981
A former special operative,
whose blood I infused

192
00:15:40,982 --> 00:15:43,485
with microscopic machines
called "nanites,"

193
00:15:43,777 --> 00:15:47,238
which she can form into anything
she can imagine.

194
00:15:47,697 --> 00:15:52,034
And, of course, you're familiar with
my flying armored forces, the Raptors.

195
00:15:52,035 --> 00:15:56,998
All together, they're an unstoppable force
we call PlanetWatch.

196
00:15:58,416 --> 00:16:01,836
More than capable of containing
any otherworldly threat.

197
00:16:04,297 --> 00:16:06,465
So you want the Defense Department

198
00:16:06,466 --> 00:16:10,052
to hire your metahumans
to take down the Kryptonian?

199
00:16:10,053 --> 00:16:13,722
After Superman acted with violence
against our Boravian allies,

200
00:16:13,723 --> 00:16:14,848
I think it'd be worth considering.

201
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:16,809
Big Blue stopped a war.

202
00:16:16,810 --> 00:16:18,602
Naive, maybe, but well-intentioned.

203
00:16:18,603 --> 00:16:23,107
Well, I don't know the intentions
of an unattended firehose, General Flag.

204
00:16:23,108 --> 00:16:25,485
I just do what I can not to be splashed.

205
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:28,487
- Mr. Luthor...
- The disarming Director Crawley.

206
00:16:28,488 --> 00:16:30,572
The country
of Boravia has purchased

207
00:16:30,573 --> 00:16:32,825
over 80 billion dollars' worth of arms

208
00:16:32,826 --> 00:16:34,994
from LuthorCorp in the past two years.

209
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:36,787
- And?
- And no one would profit more

210
00:16:36,788 --> 00:16:39,581
from a war with Boravia
and Jarhanpur than you.

211
00:16:39,582 --> 00:16:41,960
A cynic might say that having
Superman out of the way

212
00:16:42,085 --> 00:16:43,335
might not be bad for business.

213
00:16:43,336 --> 00:16:46,339
Well, what's particularly
bad for business is dying.

214
00:16:46,631 --> 00:16:49,466
And I have a distinct feeling
that's where we're all headed

215
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:51,009
with the Kryptonian running wild.

216
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,345
So we're gonna lock up all metahumans now?

217
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:55,806
Look, other metahumans
aren't going off half-cocked,

218
00:16:55,807 --> 00:16:57,599
interfering in foreign affairs.

219
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,935
They don't have--
And I have proof of this--

220
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:02,521
a hidden headquarters in Antarctica

221
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:05,233
that violates 12 international treaties.

222
00:17:05,358 --> 00:17:08,444
And they aren't aliens.

223
00:17:08,445 --> 00:17:11,196
Shouldn't all that be
more than enough reason

224
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:15,909
for PlanetWatch to at least bring
the Kryptonian in for questioning?

225
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,036
Admittedly, I'm not comfortable

226
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:21,999
with a being from another planet
as dangerous as him on the loose.

227
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,461
But the optics? Superman is popular.

228
00:17:24,586 --> 00:17:27,045
Less so every day,
according to chatter online.

229
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:30,007
Not to mention the potential risk
of failing to contain him.

230
00:17:30,008 --> 00:17:32,468
I assure you, Secretary,
we can contain him.

231
00:17:32,469 --> 00:17:34,678
Yeah, they got this stuff, uh...

232
00:17:34,679 --> 00:17:36,054
What's this
Kryptonite stuff called?

233
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:38,849
- It's called Kryptonite.
- Well, it kills him, right?

234
00:17:38,850 --> 00:17:40,976
As far as we can ascertain,
there's none left on the planet.

235
00:17:40,977 --> 00:17:42,811
I have a workaround for that as well.

236
00:17:42,812 --> 00:17:44,563
You know what? It doesn't matter, Lex.

237
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:46,607
Because without solid proof
of malicious intent,

238
00:17:46,608 --> 00:17:47,984
it's just not worth the risk.

239
00:18:27,357 --> 00:18:28,941
What are you doing here?

240
00:18:28,942 --> 00:18:30,734
Three months ago, we had our first date.

241
00:18:30,735 --> 00:18:34,571
And so, to celebrate,
I am making you your favorite:

242
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:36,073
breakfast for dinner.

243
00:18:36,074 --> 00:18:37,492
That's your favorite.

244
00:18:38,034 --> 00:18:39,117
You love breakfast.

245
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:41,955
Yeah, for breakfast.
You love it for dinner.

246
00:19:01,391 --> 00:19:03,308
- What?
- It was very funny today.

247
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:04,393
- What?
- It was hilarious,

248
00:19:04,394 --> 00:19:05,811
the little back-and-forth we had going.

249
00:19:05,812 --> 00:19:06,562
Mm.

250
00:19:06,563 --> 00:19:08,689
You giving me guff for my article.

251
00:19:08,690 --> 00:19:10,440
Jimmy was eating it up.

252
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:13,944
I wasn't acting, Clark.
If you keep interviewing yourself,

253
00:19:13,945 --> 00:19:16,572
eventually people
are gonna figure it out.

254
00:19:16,573 --> 00:19:17,990
But the glasses.

255
00:19:17,991 --> 00:19:20,576
Yeah, they won't fool everyone forever.

256
00:19:20,577 --> 00:19:25,205
And ethically, these interviews
are hugely problematic.

257
00:19:25,206 --> 00:19:28,209
I mean, y-you literally know
the questions in advance.

258
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:30,503
Okay, so I'll let you interview me.

259
00:19:31,129 --> 00:19:32,838
I'm pretty sure
you wouldn't like that.

260
00:19:32,839 --> 00:19:34,840
Come on, Lois. I'm media savvy.

261
00:19:34,841 --> 00:19:38,386
I can handle any question
that comes my way.

262
00:19:38,511 --> 00:19:40,138
Are you being serious right now?

263
00:19:40,930 --> 00:19:41,806
Yeah.

264
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:44,684
You'd let me interview you as Superman?

265
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:47,353
Sure.

266
00:19:48,771 --> 00:19:49,772
How about now?

267
00:19:52,901 --> 00:19:53,860
Um...

268
00:19:56,529 --> 00:19:57,280
Ready?

269
00:19:57,739 --> 00:19:59,198
Let's do it, Cronkite.

270
00:20:00,158 --> 00:20:01,242
Superman.

271
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:03,286
Miss Lane.

272
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:05,370
Recently, you've come under

273
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:06,414
a lot of fire for what some might--

274
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:07,456
I don't know
if it's a lot of fire, but--

275
00:20:07,457 --> 00:20:08,790
It's a lot.

276
00:20:08,791 --> 00:20:10,126
Today the Secretary of Defense

277
00:20:10,251 --> 00:20:12,502
said he was gonna look into
your actions in Boravia.

278
00:20:12,503 --> 00:20:14,713
That-- That's funny?

279
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:17,633
It's not "funny" funny, it's just, um...

280
00:20:17,634 --> 00:20:20,261
I mean, come on. My actions?
I stopped a war.

281
00:20:20,845 --> 00:20:22,888
- Maybe.
- Uh, not "maybe." I did.

282
00:20:22,889 --> 00:20:24,848
Okay. How?

283
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:27,684
Well, Boravia invaded Jarhanpur,

284
00:20:27,685 --> 00:20:29,937
and I showed up and told them
that wasn't right.

285
00:20:29,938 --> 00:20:30,687
And?

286
00:20:30,688 --> 00:20:33,023
And... smashed some tanks and things

287
00:20:33,024 --> 00:20:35,985
and a couple of planes
and some other stuff.

288
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:39,446
There were no casualties
and no significant injuries.

289
00:20:39,447 --> 00:20:40,572
Did you interact at all

290
00:20:40,573 --> 00:20:43,034
with the President of Boravia,
Vasil Ghurkos?

291
00:20:43,409 --> 00:20:44,409
A very small amount.

292
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:45,912
What's a very small amount?

293
00:20:46,788 --> 00:20:47,830
That was between us.

294
00:20:50,792 --> 00:20:52,001
This is all on the record.

295
00:20:52,126 --> 00:20:55,545
Yeah, but that conversation
was between the two of us.

296
00:20:55,546 --> 00:20:57,506
Yeah, and I would
ask that question

297
00:20:57,507 --> 00:20:59,257
whether or not
I knew the answer to it.

298
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:00,760
- Really?
- Really.

299
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:04,389
After I stopped the war,

300
00:21:05,223 --> 00:21:06,431
I went to see Ghurkos.

301
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:07,516
Where?

302
00:21:07,517 --> 00:21:09,643
In the capital of Luchebic,
at the Royal Palace.

303
00:21:09,644 --> 00:21:10,394
And?

304
00:21:10,395 --> 00:21:12,646
And I took a private audience
with Ghurkos.

305
00:21:12,647 --> 00:21:13,522
How?

306
00:21:13,523 --> 00:21:16,150
I flew him out to the desert, and I...

307
00:21:16,818 --> 00:21:17,985
And you...

308
00:21:17,986 --> 00:21:20,029
And I placed him
against a cactus.

309
00:21:20,405 --> 00:21:21,738
A cactus?

310
00:21:21,739 --> 00:21:23,824
So... torture?

311
00:21:23,825 --> 00:21:24,783
No. Not torture.

312
00:21:24,784 --> 00:21:26,911
Its spikes were like...
not even that big.

313
00:21:27,203 --> 00:21:28,203
What did you say?

314
00:21:28,204 --> 00:21:31,123
I told him that if he ever
messes with Jarhanpur again,

315
00:21:31,124 --> 00:21:32,791
he'll have to
personally answer to me.

316
00:21:32,792 --> 00:21:34,252
What did you mean by that?

317
00:21:34,377 --> 00:21:35,836
That if such events occurred,

318
00:21:35,837 --> 00:21:38,422
we would have a more serious
discussion, that's all.

319
00:21:38,423 --> 00:21:40,966
More serious than
tearing up his back on a cactus?

320
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:42,175
Ghurkos was gonna kill people.

321
00:21:42,176 --> 00:21:43,552
You seem to keep
forgetting that--

322
00:21:43,553 --> 00:21:46,138
So, in effect,
you illegally entered a country,

323
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:47,556
inserting yourself in the middle

324
00:21:47,557 --> 00:21:48,849
- of an incredibly heated...
- No, no, no. Hold on.

325
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:49,933
- geopolitical situation...
- Hold on a second.

326
00:21:49,934 --> 00:21:51,560
...siding with a nation, Jarhanpur,

327
00:21:51,561 --> 00:21:53,020
which historically has not been

328
00:21:53,021 --> 00:21:54,604
- a friend to the US...
- Jarhanpur has changed.

329
00:21:54,605 --> 00:21:56,481
...against a nation
that's technically our ally,

330
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:58,734
and then threatened
to murder their head of state.

331
00:21:58,735 --> 00:22:01,403
First of all, whether or not
Jarhanpur is an imperfect country

332
00:22:01,404 --> 00:22:03,280
does not give another nation
the right to invade it.

333
00:22:03,281 --> 00:22:04,698
Yes, but the Boravian government
maintains

334
00:22:04,699 --> 00:22:06,283
they're freeing the Jarhanpurians

335
00:22:06,284 --> 00:22:07,409
from a tyrannical regime.

336
00:22:07,410 --> 00:22:09,119
Yes, but you know that's very silly.

337
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,037
I do?

338
00:22:10,038 --> 00:22:13,206
The Boravian government,
of all people, is saying this?

339
00:22:13,207 --> 00:22:13,999
Come on!

340
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,668
This is on the record,
Superman.

341
00:22:15,793 --> 00:22:17,127
Now-- No. Now, see...

342
00:22:17,128 --> 00:22:18,587
Now you're being
dishonest, Lois.

343
00:22:18,588 --> 00:22:20,423
How am I being dishonest?

344
00:22:21,716 --> 00:22:23,300
- What are you--? Stop.
- Where's the button?

345
00:22:23,301 --> 00:22:25,427
You're being dishonest
because you know as well as I do

346
00:22:25,428 --> 00:22:26,970
that the Boravian government
is not well-intentioned.

347
00:22:26,971 --> 00:22:30,432
I think that's almost certainly
the case, but do I know that?

348
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:31,476
No, I don't.

349
00:22:32,894 --> 00:22:34,020
Can we go on now?

350
00:22:34,687 --> 00:22:35,729
Yeah, fine.

351
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:36,981
- I don't-- You do it.
- I...

352
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:40,735
You think this is going well?

353
00:22:41,027 --> 00:22:43,196
Do I think this is going well?
Um...

354
00:22:44,197 --> 00:22:45,615
I think I'm doing a good job.

355
00:22:48,326 --> 00:22:50,077
Superman, did you consult
with the President

356
00:22:50,078 --> 00:22:51,495
before entering
Boravian airspace?

357
00:22:53,498 --> 00:22:54,748
- No.
- The Secretary of Defense?

358
00:22:54,749 --> 00:22:56,542
- No.
- Or any US official

359
00:22:56,667 --> 00:22:58,376
before you took matters
into your own hands

360
00:22:58,377 --> 00:23:00,253
and decided unilaterally
how to handle

361
00:23:00,254 --> 00:23:01,338
this extremely delicate
situation?

362
00:23:01,339 --> 00:23:04,049
Ghurkos and his goons
were going to kill people.

363
00:23:04,050 --> 00:23:05,425
Yes, but the results

364
00:23:05,426 --> 00:23:07,636
of you seemingly acting
as a representative

365
00:23:07,637 --> 00:23:08,596
of the United States
will cause...

366
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:09,638
I wasn't representing
anybody...

367
00:23:09,639 --> 00:23:10,430
...more problems
around the world.

368
00:23:10,431 --> 00:23:11,264
...except for me, and-and...

369
00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:13,266
- More than a war that lasted...
- ...myself and, and, and...

370
00:23:13,267 --> 00:23:14,142
...between 12 and 24 hours...

371
00:23:14,143 --> 00:23:15,102
...good, I don't know,
doing good.

372
00:23:15,103 --> 00:23:16,520
...and was just replacing

373
00:23:16,521 --> 00:23:18,021
one tyrannical regime
with another?

374
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:19,397
Is that really how you feel?

375
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:22,610
I'm not the one being
interviewed, Superman, but...

376
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:24,986
I question it.

377
00:23:24,987 --> 00:23:27,739
Yeah, I would question myself
in the same situation

378
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:30,450
and hold off a beat
and consider the consequences.

379
00:23:30,451 --> 00:23:32,537
People were going to die!

380
00:23:42,630 --> 00:23:45,383
Okay, I'd like to
change the subject, if I could.

381
00:23:46,175 --> 00:23:47,259
Okay.

382
00:23:47,260 --> 00:23:49,469
You've gotten a lot of heat
on social media lately.

383
00:23:49,470 --> 00:23:50,595
I don't read that stuff.

384
00:23:50,596 --> 00:23:52,765
Superman doesn't have
time for selfies.

385
00:23:54,183 --> 00:23:55,433
- Third person?
- Hmm?

386
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:57,477
You're referring to yourself
in the third person now?

387
00:23:57,478 --> 00:23:58,770
No, it was just a thing
I came up with

388
00:23:58,771 --> 00:24:00,814
that I thought I'd try to work
into the next interview.

389
00:24:00,815 --> 00:24:02,149
This is on the record, Superman.

390
00:24:02,150 --> 00:24:03,775
Okay, well, not the part
where I said that.

391
00:24:03,776 --> 00:24:06,319
- Yes, that part.
- No, that part was an aside.

392
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:07,320
That was off the record.

393
00:24:07,321 --> 00:24:10,157
You have to say "off the record"
beforehand, not after.

394
00:24:10,158 --> 00:24:11,700
Why are you being like this?

395
00:24:11,701 --> 00:24:13,034
Fine, I-I won't write

396
00:24:13,035 --> 00:24:15,495
that you spend your spare time
trying to think up soundbites.

397
00:24:15,496 --> 00:24:16,873
Which are terrible, by the way.

398
00:24:17,623 --> 00:24:19,207
- Social media.
- Yes.

399
00:24:19,208 --> 00:24:21,335
As you may know,
or maybe you don't,

400
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:23,211
since you claim not to read
any of that stuff--

401
00:24:23,212 --> 00:24:24,087
Very seldomly.

402
00:24:24,088 --> 00:24:25,839
Maybe sometimes people
catch you reading it

403
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:27,465
and looking very upset.

404
00:24:27,466 --> 00:24:29,134
Okay, well, you can't use that.

405
00:24:29,135 --> 00:24:32,263
People on social media are
suspicious because you are...

406
00:24:32,972 --> 00:24:34,472
...an alien, yes?

407
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:35,557
Yes.

408
00:24:35,558 --> 00:24:38,144
I've been very honest
about that. From the beginning.

409
00:24:38,811 --> 00:24:40,521
I come from
a planet called Krypton.

410
00:24:40,855 --> 00:24:43,148
- Okay.
- Which is gone now, by the way.

411
00:24:43,149 --> 00:24:45,735
Destroyed.
Along with all of my history.

412
00:24:46,402 --> 00:24:47,569
My parents.

413
00:24:47,570 --> 00:24:49,487
They sent me here as a baby
to save my life.

414
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:50,614
Here, where?

415
00:24:50,615 --> 00:24:52,783
I'm not gonna say that.
You know I'm not gonna say that.

416
00:24:55,453 --> 00:24:56,329
Okay.

417
00:24:59,582 --> 00:25:02,710
What do you know about these
biological parents of yours?

418
00:25:03,044 --> 00:25:06,464
Just that they sent me here
to serve humanity

419
00:25:07,423 --> 00:25:09,966
and to help the world
to be a better place.

420
00:25:09,967 --> 00:25:12,094
- They said that?
- They did.

421
00:25:13,304 --> 00:25:15,348
They sent a message
along with me.

422
00:25:17,934 --> 00:25:20,060
That message
is why I do what I do.

423
00:25:20,061 --> 00:25:21,854
I cherish it more than anything.

424
00:25:22,730 --> 00:25:24,606
Because you understand now,

425
00:25:24,607 --> 00:25:26,816
there are an awful lot of people
out there maintaining

426
00:25:26,817 --> 00:25:30,070
you're here
for more nefarious purposes.

427
00:25:30,071 --> 00:25:32,281
Hashtag Superspy.
Hashtag Supershit.

428
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:33,949
Supershit!? Come on, Lois!

429
00:25:33,950 --> 00:25:35,617
You know that one
specifically irritates me!

430
00:25:35,618 --> 00:25:37,869
This is on the record, Clark!

431
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:38,870
I didn't make it up.

432
00:25:38,871 --> 00:25:40,957
It's what people on the Internet
are saying.

433
00:25:41,415 --> 00:25:42,666
I'm gonna go.

434
00:25:42,667 --> 00:25:44,543
- Really?
- Yeah.

435
00:25:44,669 --> 00:25:46,586
Come on, Clark. Don't do this.

436
00:25:46,587 --> 00:25:47,796
I'm not doing anything.

437
00:25:47,797 --> 00:25:49,798
No? No, that's not you,
packing up your shit

438
00:25:49,799 --> 00:25:51,341
and walking out of an interview?

439
00:25:51,342 --> 00:25:52,634
I'm not walking out
of an interview,

440
00:25:52,635 --> 00:25:53,802
- I'm just-- It's late.
- No, this is what you do

441
00:25:53,803 --> 00:25:55,011
every time
you're faced with conflict.

442
00:25:55,012 --> 00:25:56,304
- I'm not doing anything.
- You get mad. You pout.

443
00:25:56,305 --> 00:25:57,472
- Then you pretend...
- I'm not mad.

444
00:25:57,473 --> 00:25:59,057
- ...like nothing's wrong.
- Nothing is wrong.

445
00:25:59,058 --> 00:26:01,142
Look, I gave you
a nice, long interview.

446
00:26:01,143 --> 00:26:03,436
Longer than I ever gave myself,
by the way.

447
00:26:03,437 --> 00:26:06,022
Oh, you can time your imaginary
interviews with yourself?

448
00:26:06,023 --> 00:26:07,148
That's a thing you can do?

449
00:26:07,149 --> 00:26:08,484
You got a lot of good stuff.

450
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:10,819
Some stuff you can't use.

451
00:26:10,820 --> 00:26:12,655
I am well aware.

452
00:26:13,656 --> 00:26:15,074
I knew this would never work.

453
00:26:16,617 --> 00:26:17,702
What does that mean?

454
00:26:21,122 --> 00:26:22,039
Lois?

455
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:25,793
- What does that mean?
- Nothing, I just...

456
00:26:26,294 --> 00:26:28,545
I told you
I wasn't good at relationships.

457
00:26:33,217 --> 00:26:34,176
Okay.

458
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:06,959
The real Antarctica!

459
00:27:07,084 --> 00:27:08,669
So cool!

460
00:27:16,010 --> 00:27:17,219
It was right ahead.

461
00:27:17,887 --> 00:27:19,555
But how are we going to gain access?

462
00:27:20,473 --> 00:27:22,558
Oh, ye of little faith.

463
00:27:28,689 --> 00:27:30,441
Oh, wow!

464
00:27:43,579 --> 00:27:45,538
Oh, my God!

465
00:27:59,178 --> 00:28:01,806
Superman, I preemptively
put up the soothing--

466
00:28:02,431 --> 00:28:05,518
Oh, my. I do apologize,
but this is a restricted area.

467
00:28:07,311 --> 00:28:09,063
Wait. Can we talk--

468
00:29:10,207 --> 00:29:11,584
This is what we came for.

469
00:29:13,085 --> 00:29:14,210
Hopefully,
there's something on here

470
00:29:14,211 --> 00:29:15,670
we can use
to convince the general

471
00:29:15,671 --> 00:29:18,174
Superman requires immediate action.

472
00:29:18,883 --> 00:29:21,844
I can't stand the metahumans,
but he's so much worse.

473
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:24,680
Super... man.

474
00:29:25,931 --> 00:29:27,683
He's not a man. He's an it.

475
00:29:28,517 --> 00:29:30,935
A thing with a cocky grin
and a stupid outfit

476
00:29:30,936 --> 00:29:32,228
that's somehow become the focal point

477
00:29:32,229 --> 00:29:34,356
of the entire world's conversation.

478
00:29:35,941 --> 00:29:37,735
Nothing's felt right
since he showed up.

479
00:29:38,736 --> 00:29:40,278
I know, Lex.

480
00:29:40,279 --> 00:29:43,908
I've sacrificed my own humanity
to help get rid of it.

481
00:29:44,575 --> 00:29:45,618
Can you get in?

482
00:29:50,998 --> 00:29:52,249
Might take a while.

483
00:29:52,708 --> 00:29:53,959
What if the Kryptonian shows up?

484
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:55,127
Don't worry.

485
00:29:55,461 --> 00:29:58,047
I'm creating a... distraction.

486
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:40,881
What?

487
00:30:41,298 --> 00:30:42,424
This message...

488
00:30:43,050 --> 00:30:44,593
...from his parents.

489
00:30:45,511 --> 00:30:47,095
It's damaged, but there's more.

490
00:30:47,096 --> 00:30:48,931
It's...

491
00:30:49,723 --> 00:30:50,974
I can recover the rest.

492
00:31:12,496 --> 00:31:14,497
Whoa! Got it!

493
00:31:14,498 --> 00:31:15,666
Let it out!

494
00:31:25,301 --> 00:31:27,428
It's an awfully small distraction.

495
00:31:27,928 --> 00:31:29,138
It'll get bigger.

496
00:31:46,238 --> 00:31:47,489
Get! Go!

497
00:31:52,453 --> 00:31:54,079
Get! Get outta here!

498
00:32:42,169 --> 00:32:43,211
The giant animal

499
00:32:43,212 --> 00:32:44,962
was first spotted early this morning

500
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:48,049
in a Jitters coffee shop
about seven feet tall,

501
00:32:48,050 --> 00:32:49,968
but it has apparently been growing.

502
00:33:00,145 --> 00:33:02,356
Everybody okay?

503
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:08,070
Hey, buddy. Eyes up here.

504
00:33:46,734 --> 00:33:49,445
Deep, slow breaths, ma'am.
You're gonna be fine.

505
00:34:02,499 --> 00:34:04,960
Everybody, clear the area.

506
00:34:07,004 --> 00:34:09,297
He's just so cheap, like, so obnoxious.

507
00:34:09,298 --> 00:34:10,548
You know what I mean?

508
00:34:11,842 --> 00:34:13,718
You can afford
$1,000 concert tickets...

509
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:15,803
Finally a bit of good news
amid the chaos here this morning.

510
00:34:15,804 --> 00:34:18,723
The Justice Gang
has arrived on the scene.

511
00:34:18,724 --> 00:34:21,934
That's Green Lantern, Hawkgirl
and Mr. Terrific.

512
00:34:21,935 --> 00:34:24,021
They're funded
by the LordTech corporation.

513
00:34:24,396 --> 00:34:25,314
Get him!

514
00:34:31,653 --> 00:34:32,488
Hey!

515
00:34:59,139 --> 00:35:00,641
Heel, boy!

516
00:35:10,192 --> 00:35:11,818
- What's the skinny?
- Its hide is tough,

517
00:35:11,819 --> 00:35:13,736
but, uh, it's off balance.

518
00:35:13,737 --> 00:35:14,737
I've been trying to figure out a way

519
00:35:14,738 --> 00:35:15,948
to get it out of here alive.

520
00:35:16,323 --> 00:35:18,157
Get it someplace
where we can study it.

521
00:35:18,158 --> 00:35:20,785
- Oh, come on, man.
- What?

522
00:35:20,786 --> 00:35:23,205
Go for its eyes!

523
00:35:39,930 --> 00:35:43,224
My knee! Guy, help!

524
00:35:43,225 --> 00:35:44,935
I made giant oven mitts!

525
00:35:45,477 --> 00:35:47,729
Good for you, asshole!
I'm getting blinked to death!

526
00:36:03,328 --> 00:36:04,746
Come on, be careful!

527
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:14,422
Oh!

528
00:36:14,423 --> 00:36:16,757
Good gosh! There's gotta be
a better way to do this.

529
00:36:42,576 --> 00:36:44,119
Come on.

530
00:37:03,555 --> 00:37:05,222
Authorities are
saying there haven't been

531
00:37:05,223 --> 00:37:06,891
any signs yet of loss of life,

532
00:37:06,892 --> 00:37:09,393
thanks to Metropolis
hometown hero, Superman,

533
00:37:09,394 --> 00:37:12,021
but the damage to property
could be in the millions.

534
00:37:12,022 --> 00:37:12,939
City spokespeople...

535
00:37:12,940 --> 00:37:15,691
How's it going with that guy
you were seeing?

536
00:37:15,692 --> 00:37:17,986
You were saying
you weren't sure about it?

537
00:37:18,862 --> 00:37:20,530
Yeah. He's...

538
00:37:21,281 --> 00:37:23,075
a little strange.

539
00:37:29,623 --> 00:37:33,168
Ooh!
Kaiju steaks all around, huh?

540
00:37:33,293 --> 00:37:34,877
I was hoping we could capture it

541
00:37:34,878 --> 00:37:36,921
and take it
to an intergalactic zoo or...

542
00:37:38,090 --> 00:37:40,007
...at least euthanize it
less painfully.

543
00:37:40,008 --> 00:37:41,927
Come on, bro.
Don't be such a wuss.

544
00:37:42,511 --> 00:37:45,596
'Ey! Just another day in
the life of the Justice Gang!

545
00:37:45,597 --> 00:37:46,722
Not our name.

546
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:47,932
It's just a working name.

547
00:37:47,933 --> 00:37:49,642
Could very well prove
to be permanent though.

548
00:37:49,643 --> 00:37:51,852
- Probably not!
- Good chance though, I'm saying.

549
00:37:51,853 --> 00:37:53,354
You okay? Everybody okay?

550
00:37:53,355 --> 00:37:54,481
Just like to say thank you

551
00:37:54,606 --> 00:37:57,441
on behalf of LordTech Industries
for the opportunity--

552
00:37:59,486 --> 00:38:00,736
Why is nobody clapping?

553
00:38:08,662 --> 00:38:09,663
Come here.

554
00:38:10,747 --> 00:38:12,415
This has to be BS.

555
00:38:14,793 --> 00:38:16,127
Well, they couldn't
be mistaken?

556
00:38:16,128 --> 00:38:16,877
Oh, no.

557
00:38:16,878 --> 00:38:19,380
Well, that sounds very disturbing, Lex.

558
00:38:19,381 --> 00:38:20,965
Twenty-eight
of the world's top linguists

559
00:38:20,966 --> 00:38:23,300
have confirmed the translation

560
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:25,469
and 30 of the top forensic
computer techs

561
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:28,556
have confirmed the validity
of the footage itself.

562
00:38:28,557 --> 00:38:30,141
Any chance they're mistaken?

563
00:38:30,142 --> 00:38:32,644
Unfortunately, no.

564
00:38:33,311 --> 00:38:34,645
- You have the footage?
- Yes.

565
00:38:34,646 --> 00:38:35,604
Let's take a look.

566
00:38:37,649 --> 00:38:40,110
We love you
more than heaven, our son.

567
00:38:40,235 --> 00:38:41,737
We love you more than land.

568
00:38:42,612 --> 00:38:45,866
Our beloved home
is soon to be gone forever.

569
00:38:46,700 --> 00:38:48,451
But hope vitalizes our hearts,

570
00:38:48,452 --> 00:38:50,912
and that hope is you, Kal-El.

571
00:38:52,664 --> 00:38:53,789
We have searched
the universe

572
00:38:53,790 --> 00:38:55,792
for a home where you can do the most good.

573
00:38:56,585 --> 00:38:58,627
And live out Krypton's truth.

574
00:38:58,628 --> 00:39:00,087
That place is Earth.

575
00:39:00,088 --> 00:39:01,548
I don't get it. What's bad about that?

576
00:39:05,010 --> 00:39:07,094
The people there are simple

577
00:39:07,095 --> 00:39:09,056
and profoundly confused.

578
00:39:10,432 --> 00:39:13,017
Weak of mind
and spirit and body.

579
00:39:14,603 --> 00:39:16,145
Lord over the planet

580
00:39:16,146 --> 00:39:17,856
as the last son of Krypton.

581
00:39:20,150 --> 00:39:21,275
Dispatch of anyone

582
00:39:21,276 --> 00:39:23,820
unable or unwilling to serve you, Kal-EI.

583
00:39:25,572 --> 00:39:27,907
Take as many wives as you can,

584
00:39:27,908 --> 00:39:31,035
so your genes and Krypton's
might and legacy

585
00:39:31,036 --> 00:39:32,996
will live on
in this new frontier.

586
00:39:35,373 --> 00:39:37,459
Do us proud, our beloved son.

587
00:39:37,584 --> 00:39:39,377
Rule without mercy.

588
00:39:41,588 --> 00:39:42,713
But what about all the kind acts

589
00:39:42,714 --> 00:39:44,715
Superman has performed
over the years,

590
00:39:44,716 --> 00:39:46,593
saving countless lives?

591
00:39:46,718 --> 00:39:49,846
No. He's grooming us.

592
00:39:50,305 --> 00:39:52,348
Lulling us into complacency,

593
00:39:52,349 --> 00:39:55,059
so he can dominate without resistance,

594
00:39:55,060 --> 00:39:56,685
forging a path for his

595
00:39:56,686 --> 00:39:59,189
super-powered descendants
to rule the Earth.

596
00:40:00,232 --> 00:40:05,737
I will not accept that. Will you?

597
00:40:08,782 --> 00:40:11,409
- You seem upset.
- I'm...

598
00:40:13,286 --> 00:40:14,162
I'm scared.

599
00:40:14,704 --> 00:40:16,706
I will admit that, I am scared.

600
00:40:17,207 --> 00:40:23,130
Because who knows how large
his secret harem is already?

601
00:40:44,401 --> 00:40:48,612
Oh, hell no!
Let me in! I'm serious!

602
00:40:53,618 --> 00:40:55,161
Dude, you got a secret harem?

603
00:40:55,162 --> 00:40:56,704
No, Guy, of course
I don't have a harem.

604
00:40:56,705 --> 00:40:59,582
If any of that message
is even remotely true,

605
00:40:59,583 --> 00:41:02,460
then you are exactly
the kind of alien threat

606
00:41:02,586 --> 00:41:04,795
I was commandeered
by the Green Lantern Corps

607
00:41:04,796 --> 00:41:06,380
to protect this planet against.

608
00:41:06,381 --> 00:41:09,426
- Back off, Guy!
- Oh.

609
00:41:09,718 --> 00:41:12,261
Make a move, Big Blue.

610
00:41:12,262 --> 00:41:14,181
Guy, relax.

611
00:41:15,348 --> 00:41:16,892
Was the message real or not?

612
00:41:18,018 --> 00:41:20,853
The first half.
The first half is... is real.

613
00:41:20,854 --> 00:41:22,396
The second half was damaged

614
00:41:22,397 --> 00:41:24,356
in the t-trip from Krypton to Earth.

615
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:26,610
- So it's-it's gotta be doctored.
- No way, Clark.

616
00:41:27,110 --> 00:41:28,736
I know these computer forensics
guys.

617
00:41:28,737 --> 00:41:32,407
They're not gonna say it's legit
unless they are sure.

618
00:41:33,283 --> 00:41:34,825
I'm so sorry, man,

619
00:41:34,826 --> 00:41:36,703
but there's no way that message is fake.

620
00:41:37,621 --> 00:41:38,788
Where'd they get the footage
though?

621
00:41:53,011 --> 00:41:55,429
Are you considering bringing
Superman in for questioning?

622
00:41:55,430 --> 00:41:59,099
We're talking with the President,
and we are reviewing our options now.

623
00:41:59,100 --> 00:42:00,392
I'm sorry, but I have to go,
Miss Lane.

624
00:42:00,393 --> 00:42:01,603
And if you did, when would that--

625
00:42:02,270 --> 00:42:03,103
You buying this?

626
00:42:03,104 --> 00:42:04,856
I don't put anything
past Luthor, Rick.

627
00:42:05,565 --> 00:42:07,983
But the message is authentic.

628
00:42:07,984 --> 00:42:11,779
If the Kryptonian is a danger,
we have to act.

629
00:42:11,780 --> 00:42:13,364
I was a big Superman fan.

630
00:42:13,365 --> 00:42:14,865
I supported him
all the time online and stuff,

631
00:42:14,866 --> 00:42:15,991
but now?

632
00:42:15,992 --> 00:42:17,117
I mean, I hope he rots in hell.

633
00:42:17,118 --> 00:42:18,285
I don't care.
You're supposed to get out!

634
00:42:18,286 --> 00:42:19,245
Get me some pictures.

635
00:42:19,246 --> 00:42:20,287
We have a deadline!

636
00:42:20,288 --> 00:42:21,372
Where is he? Get there now!

637
00:42:21,373 --> 00:42:22,289
Don't call me Chief.

638
00:42:22,290 --> 00:42:23,833
Okay. I'm gonna do my job.

639
00:42:23,959 --> 00:42:26,085
It's no wonder the Kryptonian

640
00:42:26,086 --> 00:42:30,130
interfered with Boravia's interests.

641
00:42:30,131 --> 00:42:34,969
Boravia wants to save the people
of Jarhanpur.

642
00:42:34,970 --> 00:42:38,598
And Superman
wants to keep them enslaved!

643
00:42:39,349 --> 00:42:44,478
Also, from what I hear,

644
00:42:44,479 --> 00:42:50,651
he finds Boravian women
the most physically attractive

645
00:42:50,652 --> 00:42:55,489
and wants to add them
to his secret harem.

646
00:42:57,951 --> 00:42:59,953
I have a question,
President Ghurkos.

647
00:43:00,912 --> 00:43:01,913
Thank you.

648
00:43:03,999 --> 00:43:07,085
That couldn't
have gone better, Mr. President!

649
00:43:07,502 --> 00:43:10,171
You were so handsome and dynamic!

650
00:43:10,505 --> 00:43:11,965
Wonderful!

651
00:43:12,299 --> 00:43:14,759
Very handsome! Very handsome!

652
00:43:15,927 --> 00:43:18,596
Go! Leave me be!

653
00:43:56,843 --> 00:43:58,302
We did it, Lex!

654
00:43:58,303 --> 00:44:01,305
I wouldn't celebrate until
the alien is off the board.

655
00:44:01,306 --> 00:44:04,058
Oh, here. I brought you a donut.
From Dough's Holes.

656
00:44:04,059 --> 00:44:06,018
New shop in Park Ridge,
of all places.

657
00:44:06,019 --> 00:44:09,355
The fake message,
a stroke of genius.

658
00:44:09,356 --> 00:44:10,272
It's not fake.

659
00:44:10,273 --> 00:44:13,108
He is here to kill us. I knew it!

660
00:44:13,109 --> 00:44:14,360
At Superman's fortress,

661
00:44:14,361 --> 00:44:16,737
I hoped to get the knowledge
to help destroy him.

662
00:44:16,738 --> 00:44:18,155
Little did I know,
his own parents

663
00:44:18,156 --> 00:44:19,491
would be providing it.

664
00:44:19,991 --> 00:44:21,158
Oh.

665
00:44:21,159 --> 00:44:22,451
Right? Yeah.

666
00:44:22,452 --> 00:44:25,163
Been thinking of opening one
in my half of Jarhanpur.

667
00:44:32,712 --> 00:44:36,048
Four. Four. What happened?

668
00:44:36,049 --> 00:44:40,887
I tried to protect Superman.

669
00:44:44,724 --> 00:44:47,851
How did Luthor get in here?
It's keyed into my DNA.

670
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:51,438
Must protect Superman.

671
00:44:51,439 --> 00:44:53,900
Four.

672
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:58,488
I'm sorry, friend.

673
00:45:10,083 --> 00:45:11,042
Krypto?

674
00:45:16,214 --> 00:45:17,340
Krypto!

675
00:45:22,512 --> 00:45:23,721
Well, yeah,
that's gonna become--

676
00:45:25,890 --> 00:45:28,225
- Lex, I tried to stop him.
- It's fine, Heather.

677
00:45:28,226 --> 00:45:30,018
Superman, we finally meet.

678
00:45:30,019 --> 00:45:31,855
- Would you like a coffee or tea?
- Where's the dog?

679
00:45:32,439 --> 00:45:33,105
Dog?

680
00:45:33,106 --> 00:45:34,982
The dog, Luthor!
You took the dog!

681
00:45:34,983 --> 00:45:36,733
That's right, Eve, get all of this.

682
00:45:40,822 --> 00:45:42,781
Where's the dog?

683
00:45:42,782 --> 00:45:46,911
I have no clue
what you're talking about.

684
00:45:49,539 --> 00:45:51,875
He's just a dog.

685
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:54,418
I don't know what dog
you're talking about.

686
00:45:54,419 --> 00:45:55,753
Ugly dog in a cape?

687
00:45:56,379 --> 00:45:57,797
- What did you say?
- Hmm?

688
00:45:58,590 --> 00:46:00,341
I didn't say anything.

689
00:46:00,717 --> 00:46:01,968
You heard what he said!

690
00:46:02,093 --> 00:46:03,552
You heard him! He took him!

691
00:46:03,553 --> 00:46:05,596
I mean, it seems to me,

692
00:46:05,597 --> 00:46:09,933
that the only rabid animal
around here is Superman.

693
00:46:09,934 --> 00:46:13,353
Ever since the discovery
of the Kryptonian's master plan,

694
00:46:13,354 --> 00:46:15,689
he's gone off the deep end.
Thoughts, Chris?

695
00:46:15,690 --> 00:46:17,525
Can't say I'm surprised, Cleavis.

696
00:46:17,984 --> 00:46:19,109
It's guys like this, they always got

697
00:46:19,110 --> 00:46:20,944
a whole bunch of dark, ugly secrets.

698
00:46:20,945 --> 00:46:22,821
What do you mean,
"guys like this?"

699
00:46:22,822 --> 00:46:24,407
Thinks he's better
than everybody else.

700
00:46:25,200 --> 00:46:27,451
Makes this declaration
he's against killing people

701
00:46:27,452 --> 00:46:28,410
unless it's
absolutely necessary.

702
00:46:29,329 --> 00:46:30,079
Really, dude?

703
00:46:30,788 --> 00:46:32,623
It kinda sounds like
you're trying to make the guys

704
00:46:32,624 --> 00:46:34,667
who are a little more
edgier than you look like jerks.

705
00:46:34,792 --> 00:46:36,126
- Know what I mean?
- Mm-hmm.

706
00:46:36,127 --> 00:46:38,795
A lot of these guys, these...

707
00:46:38,796 --> 00:46:40,006
heroes from the magazines,

708
00:46:40,131 --> 00:46:41,465
they're obsessed with me.

709
00:46:41,466 --> 00:46:43,509
'Cause I'm more jacked
than they are.

710
00:46:43,510 --> 00:46:44,426
They know they don't have--

711
00:46:48,556 --> 00:46:50,058
You have a dog?

712
00:46:50,558 --> 00:46:54,187
No, not really. It's more of
a... foster situation.

713
00:47:00,944 --> 00:47:02,153
Cocoa.

714
00:47:08,785 --> 00:47:10,203
You were out there helping them?

715
00:47:14,040 --> 00:47:16,000
Oh, no, that's just, uh--

716
00:47:16,125 --> 00:47:17,293
That's just
some dimensional imp.

717
00:47:18,169 --> 00:47:20,837
They've got that handled.
I was looking for the dog.

718
00:47:28,805 --> 00:47:29,973
You okay?

719
00:47:31,099 --> 00:47:33,351
The footage is not
what it looks like, Lois.

720
00:47:34,602 --> 00:47:35,894
Okay.

721
00:47:35,895 --> 00:47:38,313
The ship my parents sent me in
was damaged in transit,

722
00:47:38,314 --> 00:47:41,067
so I only ever heard
the first part of the message.

723
00:47:42,235 --> 00:47:44,654
And I believed
I knew how it ended.

724
00:47:45,488 --> 00:47:48,657
That my parents had sent me here
to serve the people of Earth

725
00:47:48,658 --> 00:47:50,493
and to be a good man.

726
00:47:52,745 --> 00:47:55,290
I'm not here
to rule over anybody, Lois.

727
00:47:55,790 --> 00:47:59,961
I never thought you were,
even for a moment, Clark.

728
00:48:08,928 --> 00:48:10,138
Oh, that's really good.

729
00:48:11,723 --> 00:48:14,100
I'm sorry we fought.

730
00:48:15,435 --> 00:48:16,311
Me too.

731
00:48:16,769 --> 00:48:18,604
But we're bound to, though.

732
00:48:18,605 --> 00:48:20,690
We're so different.

733
00:48:21,399 --> 00:48:24,444
I was just some punk rock kid
from Bakerline, and you're...

734
00:48:25,528 --> 00:48:26,737
Superman.

735
00:48:26,738 --> 00:48:29,323
- I'm punk rock.
- You are not punk rock.

736
00:48:29,324 --> 00:48:30,907
I like the Strangle-Fellows,

737
00:48:30,908 --> 00:48:33,076
and the P.O.D.s
and the Mighty Crabjoys.

738
00:48:33,077 --> 00:48:35,662
Those are pop radio bands.
They're not punk rock.

739
00:48:35,663 --> 00:48:38,333
The Mighty Crabjoys suck.

740
00:48:38,458 --> 00:48:40,418
Okay, well,
a lot of people love 'em.

741
00:48:43,630 --> 00:48:46,674
My point is, I question
everything and everyone.

742
00:48:47,759 --> 00:48:49,926
You trust everyone

743
00:48:49,927 --> 00:48:53,264
and think everyone
you've ever met is, like...

744
00:48:54,474 --> 00:48:55,725
beautiful.

745
00:48:59,646 --> 00:49:01,689
Maybe that's the real punk rock.

746
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:14,951
Lois, what did you mean
when you said

747
00:49:14,952 --> 00:49:16,454
that you knew
this would never work?

748
00:49:19,707 --> 00:49:20,875
I don't know.

749
00:49:26,673 --> 00:49:27,714
I'm gonna go.

750
00:49:27,715 --> 00:49:29,925
The DOJ has
a warrant out for my arrest,

751
00:49:29,926 --> 00:49:32,052
so I'm gonna turn myself in.

752
00:49:32,053 --> 00:49:34,389
Wait, what? Why?

753
00:49:34,764 --> 00:49:36,807
Maybe they'll take me
wherever they took the dog.

754
00:49:36,808 --> 00:49:38,016
I don't know
how else to find him.

755
00:49:38,017 --> 00:49:39,142
It's a dog.

756
00:49:39,143 --> 00:49:41,521
Yeah, and he's not even
a very good one, but...

757
00:49:42,605 --> 00:49:44,107
he's out there alone.

758
00:49:44,816 --> 00:49:46,192
And he's probably scared.

759
00:50:03,543 --> 00:50:04,502
I love you, Lois.

760
00:50:06,129 --> 00:50:08,423
I probably should have
told you that a long time ago.

761
00:50:27,233 --> 00:50:28,900
Is that necessary?

762
00:50:28,901 --> 00:50:30,737
I'm coming in on my own accord.

763
00:50:32,822 --> 00:50:34,365
No one read me my rights.

764
00:50:34,824 --> 00:50:36,450
Courts decided
those rights don't apply

765
00:50:36,451 --> 00:50:38,244
to extraterrestrial organisms.

766
00:50:38,369 --> 00:50:39,661
Therefore,
at this point, Superman,

767
00:50:39,662 --> 00:50:41,372
you don't have
any rights to read.

768
00:50:41,789 --> 00:50:42,956
The government
is very well aware

769
00:50:42,957 --> 00:50:44,917
of the potential limitations
detaining you,

770
00:50:45,042 --> 00:50:46,585
so we've outsourced
your confinement

771
00:50:46,586 --> 00:50:48,920
and your interrogation
to PlanetWatch.

772
00:50:48,921 --> 00:50:50,088
PlanetWatch?

773
00:50:51,007 --> 00:50:52,633
I'm sorry about this.

774
00:51:03,436 --> 00:51:06,564
♪ Bring me sunshine
Bring me love ♪

775
00:51:07,440 --> 00:51:10,942
♪ Bring me sunshine
In your eye ♪

776
00:51:12,820 --> 00:51:16,949
♪ Bring me a rainbow
From the sky ♪

777
00:51:17,909 --> 00:51:22,746
♪ Life's too short to be spent
Having anything but fun ♪

778
00:51:24,624 --> 00:51:28,628
♪ We can be so content
If we gather little sunbeams ♪

779
00:51:28,753 --> 00:51:30,463
♪ Be light-hearted ♪

780
00:51:32,089 --> 00:51:33,673
♪ All day long ♪

781
00:51:33,674 --> 00:51:34,633
Hey!

782
00:51:34,634 --> 00:51:36,843
♪ Keep me singing
Happy songs ♪

783
00:52:00,785 --> 00:52:02,870
Twice in two days.
What a pleasure.

784
00:52:03,579 --> 00:52:04,580
Luthor.

785
00:52:05,665 --> 00:52:07,834
Your obsession with me
is getting a little creepy.

786
00:52:07,959 --> 00:52:10,836
Don't worry. Tall, dark,
and Martian isn't my type.

787
00:52:10,837 --> 00:52:12,922
- Kryptonian.
- Eh, same diff.

788
00:52:21,973 --> 00:52:23,139
Where are we?

789
00:52:23,140 --> 00:52:24,724
A pocket universe.

790
00:52:24,725 --> 00:52:27,519
I replicated the Big Bang
with a LuthorCorp mega-collider,

791
00:52:27,520 --> 00:52:30,481
tearing a tiny hole between
the two universal fabrics.

792
00:52:31,440 --> 00:52:34,360
I'm able to access it from
multiple dimensional portals

793
00:52:34,485 --> 00:52:35,652
I've set up around the globe.

794
00:52:36,571 --> 00:52:40,240
Rex, the metahuman
known as the Element Man,

795
00:52:40,241 --> 00:52:43,034
has been called into service
for a specific purpose.

796
00:52:43,035 --> 00:52:45,871
He can metamorphose
into any known substance.

797
00:52:45,872 --> 00:52:50,835
Even substances foreign
to this planet, like...

798
00:52:58,050 --> 00:52:59,844
...Kryptonite.

799
00:53:02,972 --> 00:53:05,307
Once again,
Vasil Ghurkos is sending troops

800
00:53:05,308 --> 00:53:07,183
to the Jarhanpurian border.

801
00:53:07,184 --> 00:53:08,268
Superman's been
out of commission

802
00:53:08,269 --> 00:53:10,855
less than a day, and already
Boravia's pulling this crap?

803
00:53:11,856 --> 00:53:13,189
- Right?
- What?

804
00:53:13,190 --> 00:53:14,649
Sorry, I'm trying to figure out

805
00:53:14,650 --> 00:53:16,943
how Lex Luthor's
connected to all this.

806
00:53:16,944 --> 00:53:17,944
How's that a mystery?

807
00:53:17,945 --> 00:53:20,739
LuthorCorp sells arms
to Boravia, Boravia goes to war,

808
00:53:20,740 --> 00:53:23,450
Luthor sells more arms
and gets richer than ever.

809
00:53:23,451 --> 00:53:25,201
- Nope.
- No?

810
00:53:25,202 --> 00:53:26,412
Uh-uh.

811
00:53:26,913 --> 00:53:28,580
I have a connection at BodaBank.

812
00:53:28,581 --> 00:53:31,876
Boda handles the transactions
between LuthorCorp and Boravia.

813
00:53:32,001 --> 00:53:33,335
Yes, LuthorCorp sold them

814
00:53:33,336 --> 00:53:35,295
approximately 80 billion
dollars' worth of arms,

815
00:53:35,296 --> 00:53:36,421
but for those arms,

816
00:53:36,422 --> 00:53:39,799
Boravia paid only
1.625 billion dollars.

817
00:53:39,800 --> 00:53:42,177
So Luthor gave them arms
for free? For what?

818
00:53:42,178 --> 00:53:46,890
That's the 78 billion,
375-million-dollar question.

819
00:53:46,891 --> 00:53:48,350
Have you found out
where they're holding Superman?

820
00:53:48,351 --> 00:53:50,226
No one in the government'll say.

821
00:53:50,227 --> 00:53:52,687
Luthor seems to be working
to disable Superman

822
00:53:52,688 --> 00:53:55,649
just so he can't stop
the invasion of Jarhanpur.

823
00:53:55,650 --> 00:53:56,442
Why?

824
00:53:56,984 --> 00:53:58,610
That's way too much sugar, Lois.

825
00:53:58,611 --> 00:54:01,279
I party like a rock star, choir boy.

826
00:54:01,280 --> 00:54:03,282
Still can't hide
the taste of petroleum.

827
00:54:03,699 --> 00:54:04,659
God!

828
00:54:21,801 --> 00:54:23,593
Lex is holding Superman
in a pocket universe.

829
00:54:23,594 --> 00:54:24,719
A what?

830
00:54:24,720 --> 00:54:26,012
I don't know
what a pocket universe is.

831
00:54:26,013 --> 00:54:27,222
Neither does my source.

832
00:54:27,223 --> 00:54:29,474
They don't know anything
about anything, really.

833
00:54:29,475 --> 00:54:31,643
But for sure
he's in a pocket universe.

834
00:54:31,644 --> 00:54:32,811
Who's your source?

835
00:54:32,812 --> 00:54:35,147
I can't say, but you owe me.

836
00:54:35,648 --> 00:54:36,565
Big time.

837
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:38,234
Like...

838
00:54:39,819 --> 00:54:42,071
I can't even tell you how big.

839
00:54:44,949 --> 00:54:46,992
I love you, Jimmy Olsen.

840
00:54:46,993 --> 00:54:48,535
- I love you.
- Love you.

841
00:55:02,758 --> 00:55:05,760
Just my Monkey-Bots here,
farming outrage 24/7.

842
00:55:05,761 --> 00:55:07,388
Trashing you online.

843
00:55:07,847 --> 00:55:09,472
Hashtag Supershit.

844
00:55:20,151 --> 00:55:21,485
Krypto.

845
00:55:24,196 --> 00:55:26,197
How do you contain a super dog?

846
00:55:27,450 --> 00:55:29,617
You beam super squirrels
into its brain.

847
00:55:31,495 --> 00:55:33,330
We'll learn what we can.

848
00:55:34,248 --> 00:55:37,585
Then we'll put the varmint down.

849
00:55:38,502 --> 00:55:40,254
It will undoubtedly be painful.

850
00:55:41,255 --> 00:55:43,465
Mr. Luthor, please!
I swear...

851
00:55:43,466 --> 00:55:46,302
This is our private
correctional institution.

852
00:55:46,719 --> 00:55:48,928
Yeah, most cells are
rented out to governments

853
00:55:48,929 --> 00:55:51,181
who want to keep
their incarcerations

854
00:55:51,182 --> 00:55:53,892
of political agitators private.

855
00:55:53,893 --> 00:55:56,562
Others are for more
personal transgressions.

856
00:55:56,896 --> 00:55:58,521
Fleurette wrote a blog about me.

857
00:55:58,522 --> 00:56:00,023
There are few things I hate

858
00:56:00,024 --> 00:56:02,610
more than petty ex-girlfriends.

859
00:56:03,486 --> 00:56:04,861
You wouldn't be telling me
any of this if you--

860
00:56:04,862 --> 00:56:07,363
If we ever planned
on letting you out? No.

861
00:56:08,949 --> 00:56:11,160
You'd be terminated
already if it was up to me.

862
00:56:11,577 --> 00:56:13,203
First, the government has some
questions they want answered.

863
00:56:16,916 --> 00:56:19,835
Rex. Look who it is.

864
00:56:28,594 --> 00:56:30,637
You be sure
to keep our guest in check.

865
00:56:30,638 --> 00:56:33,139
Little Joseph certainly
wouldn't want it any other way.

866
00:56:34,308 --> 00:56:36,602
I'll be back tomorrow
to get the answers we need.

867
00:56:40,940 --> 00:56:43,526
Hey, handsome.

868
00:56:47,279 --> 00:56:48,739
Come on over.

869
00:57:01,085 --> 00:57:02,961
- Hi!
- Hey, Eve.

870
00:57:02,962 --> 00:57:04,295
Oh, sorry we had to meet here,

871
00:57:04,296 --> 00:57:06,506
but Lex is always accessing
traffic cameras,

872
00:57:06,507 --> 00:57:07,382
so he knows where I am.

873
00:57:07,383 --> 00:57:09,551
I really don't understand why
you stay in that relationship.

874
00:57:09,552 --> 00:57:11,719
'Cause he made a point to tell
me about all his ex-girlfriends

875
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:13,680
he had imprisoned
in his pocket universe.

876
00:57:13,681 --> 00:57:15,265
- What?
- Right?

877
00:57:15,266 --> 00:57:17,267
- How's your mom?
- My mom?

878
00:57:17,268 --> 00:57:18,393
Oh, I love her so much.

879
00:57:18,394 --> 00:57:21,062
I think of her as my mom,
even more than my own mother.

880
00:57:21,063 --> 00:57:22,648
Oh, she feels the same way,

881
00:57:22,773 --> 00:57:24,816
from the-the one time
that you guys met.

882
00:57:24,817 --> 00:57:26,276
- Yeah?
- So, hey. Okay.

883
00:57:26,277 --> 00:57:28,069
- Yes. Yes.
- Eve?

884
00:57:28,070 --> 00:57:29,529
There seems to be
some sort of connection

885
00:57:29,530 --> 00:57:31,781
between Boravia and your boyfriend.

886
00:57:31,782 --> 00:57:32,992
- I'm not clear on what--
- Oh.

887
00:57:33,325 --> 00:57:34,118
What's wrong?

888
00:57:34,660 --> 00:57:35,828
What's "oh"?

889
00:57:36,162 --> 00:57:38,413
I thought you wanted
to see me, Jimmy.

890
00:57:38,414 --> 00:57:39,497
I do but, Eve,

891
00:57:39,498 --> 00:57:42,543
how could I even really see you
with Lex still in the picture?

892
00:57:42,668 --> 00:57:44,419
You're just trying
to get information out of me.

893
00:57:44,420 --> 00:57:45,628
I swear to God, that's not it.

894
00:57:45,629 --> 00:57:47,839
I-I just know that if I could
get some real dirt on him,

895
00:57:47,840 --> 00:57:49,465
then maybe
the two of us could--

896
00:57:49,466 --> 00:57:51,010
Could be together again?

897
00:57:56,849 --> 00:57:57,850
Yeah.

898
00:57:59,560 --> 00:58:00,768
But you said my toes look like

899
00:58:00,769 --> 00:58:02,437
someone spilled
shrimp cocktail on the floor.

900
00:58:02,438 --> 00:58:04,647
You have unconventional toes.
Who cares?

901
00:58:04,648 --> 00:58:05,857
There's other parts of you
that people would

902
00:58:05,858 --> 00:58:07,650
find very attractive.

903
00:58:07,651 --> 00:58:09,486
Lex tortured a dog the other day.

904
00:58:10,154 --> 00:58:12,197
- Jesus Christ!
- I know.

905
00:58:12,198 --> 00:58:13,949
- I have to go.
- Eve.

906
00:58:14,867 --> 00:58:16,368
Please see
what you can find out.

907
00:58:17,453 --> 00:58:19,788
- Okay.
- Yes! Yes!

908
00:58:21,123 --> 00:58:22,208
Okay.

909
00:58:24,877 --> 00:58:26,211
I'm-I'm putting 'em in my pocket.

910
00:58:26,212 --> 00:58:27,963
Okay.

911
00:58:37,973 --> 00:58:40,266
Joseph. He's your son?

912
00:58:40,267 --> 00:58:41,352
Don't talk to me.

913
00:58:42,019 --> 00:58:42,810
Please.

914
00:58:45,064 --> 00:58:48,274
I could fly over and get him
if you just--

915
00:58:48,275 --> 00:58:49,359
if you'd stop
with the Kryptonite.

916
00:58:49,360 --> 00:58:51,611
There's no way out of here,
okay? So, just...

917
00:58:51,612 --> 00:58:53,613
- There's always a way.
- I said don't talk to me!

918
00:58:54,990 --> 00:58:55,824
I told you.

919
00:58:57,952 --> 00:58:59,495
Don't talk to me!

920
00:59:09,546 --> 00:59:10,880
Yeah,
so what do you want me to do?

921
00:59:10,881 --> 00:59:11,965
Where's the creamer?

922
00:59:11,966 --> 00:59:13,883
On the counter,
where it always is.

923
00:59:13,884 --> 00:59:16,970
He's in your group, right?
The, um, uh--

924
00:59:16,971 --> 00:59:18,972
- What's it called, again?
- The Justice Gang.

925
00:59:18,973 --> 00:59:20,556
- No.
- We're not called that.

926
00:59:20,557 --> 00:59:22,058
Yeah, your name is Mr. Terrific.

927
00:59:22,059 --> 00:59:23,685
You don't get a vote
with a name like that.

928
00:59:23,686 --> 00:59:25,645
I also voted against it.

929
00:59:25,646 --> 00:59:28,731
Yes.
And as leader, I get tiebreaker.

930
00:59:28,732 --> 00:59:30,776
No, Superman
is not officially a member.

931
00:59:30,901 --> 00:59:31,526
Because you don't
want him to vote.

932
00:59:31,527 --> 00:59:32,610
You know
which way that would go.

933
00:59:32,611 --> 00:59:33,903
Shut up. He's kidding.

934
00:59:33,904 --> 00:59:37,032
So, how do you even know
Superman anyway?

935
00:59:37,992 --> 00:59:40,076
I... just... do.

936
00:59:40,077 --> 00:59:41,744
So you know
about the hypno-glasses?

937
00:59:41,745 --> 00:59:42,954
Now she does.

938
00:59:42,955 --> 00:59:46,417
I'm not saying who he is, just
that he wears hypno-glasses.

939
00:59:46,542 --> 00:59:47,375
They make his face...

940
00:59:47,376 --> 00:59:48,501
Terrific, how do they work?

941
00:59:48,502 --> 00:59:50,044
They make his face
look different

942
00:59:50,045 --> 00:59:51,629
in your brain
when he wears them.

943
00:59:51,630 --> 00:59:52,714
So that you don't know
who he is.

944
00:59:52,715 --> 00:59:54,507
Yes, I know this, first of all.

945
00:59:54,508 --> 00:59:56,467
But, second of all, you really
shouldn't be telling me this

946
00:59:56,468 --> 00:59:58,970
in case I don't know who he is.

947
00:59:58,971 --> 01:00:00,305
So, you know he's Clark Kent?

948
01:00:00,306 --> 01:00:03,266
Oh, my God.
Why does he trust everyone?

949
01:00:03,267 --> 01:00:06,979
He doesn't. Just us because
we are also of the cloth.

950
01:00:08,272 --> 01:00:09,398
"Of the cloth?"

951
01:00:11,608 --> 01:00:14,111
- What are we gonna do?
- About what?

952
01:00:14,403 --> 01:00:17,196
Superman! He's your friend!

953
01:00:17,197 --> 01:00:19,532
Some friend.
Came here to rule over me?

954
01:00:19,533 --> 01:00:21,285
It would be difficult
to find him.

955
01:00:21,869 --> 01:00:25,663
I put nanobot GPS trackers
into Superman's bloodstream.

956
01:00:25,664 --> 01:00:27,333
You can see
where his trail ends

957
01:00:27,458 --> 01:00:29,000
abruptly right here at Fort Kramer,

958
01:00:29,001 --> 01:00:31,961
a dormant military post across
the river about ten miles down.

959
01:00:31,962 --> 01:00:34,672
Even if he was dead, those
trackers would still be there.

960
01:00:34,673 --> 01:00:36,382
So, all this leads me to believe,

961
01:00:36,383 --> 01:00:37,717
as your article surmised,

962
01:00:37,718 --> 01:00:39,052
he really is in a pocket universe.

963
01:00:40,304 --> 01:00:43,473
You put nanobot GPS trackers
in your friend's bloodstream?

964
01:00:43,474 --> 01:00:45,017
Oh, I do that to everybody.

965
01:00:45,559 --> 01:00:48,144
So, okay. Come on.
Let's go to Fort Kramer then.

966
01:00:48,145 --> 01:00:49,937
The four of us,
and find out what's going on.

967
01:00:49,938 --> 01:00:52,024
And then do what?

968
01:00:52,649 --> 01:00:54,234
Save him.

969
01:00:54,735 --> 01:00:56,027
You wanna break a federally

970
01:00:56,028 --> 01:00:57,987
incarcerated prisoner
out of jail?

971
01:00:57,988 --> 01:00:59,655
Look, I think this is being done

972
01:00:59,656 --> 01:01:01,867
to keep him from interfering
with the Boravian invasion.

973
01:01:01,992 --> 01:01:04,410
No, you look.
I'm a Green Lantern, lady.

974
01:01:04,411 --> 01:01:06,996
That means I took a vow
not to get involved in politics.

975
01:01:06,997 --> 01:01:08,248
Oh, that's part of the vows?

976
01:01:08,374 --> 01:01:09,957
It's implied. Yeah.

977
01:01:09,958 --> 01:01:11,209
An implied vow?

978
01:01:11,210 --> 01:01:12,627
Every time there's something
he doesn't want to do,

979
01:01:12,628 --> 01:01:13,711
he says it's part of some vow.

980
01:01:13,712 --> 01:01:14,837
Oh, I swear to God.

981
01:01:14,838 --> 01:01:17,256
I am two seconds away
from forming a giant hammer,

982
01:01:17,257 --> 01:01:18,592
and beating you both to death.

983
01:01:19,635 --> 01:01:21,677
Is Supes here
to take over the world?

984
01:01:21,678 --> 01:01:23,096
I don't know. Probably not.

985
01:01:23,097 --> 01:01:25,014
But the risk
is just not worth the beef

986
01:01:25,015 --> 01:01:27,225
between the US government
and the Justice Gang.

987
01:01:27,226 --> 01:01:29,185
Not our name.
Makes us sound like cowboys.

988
01:01:29,186 --> 01:01:31,188
But I agree with the rest.

989
01:01:32,022 --> 01:01:33,856
So you're just gonna
let your friend rot

990
01:01:33,857 --> 01:01:35,734
in a pocket universe?

991
01:01:48,747 --> 01:01:51,166
That haircut should be
against your vows.

992
01:01:51,291 --> 01:01:52,418
That what?

993
01:01:53,377 --> 01:01:54,961
That what should be what?

994
01:01:54,962 --> 01:01:58,882
I'll have you know
348 chicks say otherwise.

995
01:02:04,763 --> 01:02:05,514
Hey!

996
01:02:08,600 --> 01:02:09,268
What?

997
01:02:09,643 --> 01:02:11,478
I'm not saying
we're gonna save him, but...

998
01:02:12,521 --> 01:02:14,272
...I think we can at least
check out what's going on

999
01:02:14,273 --> 01:02:16,232
with your boyfriend
at this Fort Kramer.

1000
01:02:16,233 --> 01:02:17,151
He's not--

1001
01:02:18,235 --> 01:02:19,570
We're just seeing each other.

1002
01:02:20,529 --> 01:02:21,280
But thanks.

1003
01:02:21,822 --> 01:02:22,906
You want me to drive?

1004
01:02:25,075 --> 01:02:26,410
We'll take my ride.

1005
01:02:46,930 --> 01:02:48,222
You have a flying saucer,

1006
01:02:48,223 --> 01:02:50,434
but you couldn't get
a faster garage door?

1007
01:02:51,310 --> 01:02:52,686
I haven't worked on that yet.

1008
01:02:54,688 --> 01:02:57,191
I'm not even sure how I feel.
Honestly.

1009
01:02:57,691 --> 01:03:00,110
- What?
- About Clark.

1010
01:03:00,569 --> 01:03:01,986
He's not my boyfriend.

1011
01:03:01,987 --> 01:03:03,237
We've actually just been
seeing each other...

1012
01:03:03,238 --> 01:03:05,448
- Yeah, lady, just to be clear,
- ...for a couple of months--

1013
01:03:05,449 --> 01:03:06,992
I'm not into people's emotions.

1014
01:03:07,117 --> 01:03:08,660
Yeah, no, totally.

1015
01:03:09,161 --> 01:03:10,370
I'm just thinking out loud.

1016
01:03:10,996 --> 01:03:12,622
I was gonna
break up with him, actually.

1017
01:03:12,623 --> 01:03:14,374
I mean, we had this huge fight,

1018
01:03:14,500 --> 01:03:17,002
and he told me he loved me,
and it just didn't...

1019
01:03:26,053 --> 01:03:28,430
Q&A time, alien.

1020
01:03:32,476 --> 01:03:34,310
Today we have a special guest.

1021
01:03:34,311 --> 01:03:37,523
