1275
01:21:51,657 --> 01:21:52,742
Uh-huh.

1276
01:21:53,451 --> 01:21:54,868
How do you do it, Jimmy?

1277
01:21:54,869 --> 01:21:56,202
Look, I didn't even want to bother you,

1278
01:21:56,203 --> 01:21:58,038
but you told me to call
with anything I got, so I--

1279
01:21:58,039 --> 01:22:00,166
Yeah, but I thought you said
she disappeared off the line.

1280
01:22:00,499 --> 01:22:02,417
I don't know. She might have
dropped her phone in the toilet.

1281
01:22:02,418 --> 01:22:04,336
She does that a lot.

1282
01:22:04,337 --> 01:22:07,840
Well, I'm not really sure
that sexy selfies are--

1283
01:22:19,644 --> 01:22:21,479
Your hot ex is a genius.

1284
01:22:21,937 --> 01:22:23,688
- Hot?
- We have to talk to Perry.

1285
01:22:23,689 --> 01:22:25,524
I'll be there as soon as I can, okay?

1286
01:22:28,194 --> 01:22:31,321
Sending sexy selfies
behind the back of Lex Luthor?

1287
01:22:31,322 --> 01:22:33,824
She has to be the biggest idiot
in the world.

1288
01:22:34,367 --> 01:22:36,910
Lex, he just told you,
the portal was destroyed!

1289
01:22:36,911 --> 01:22:38,286
The dimensional aperture
is still there...

1290
01:22:38,287 --> 01:22:39,079
Syd, tell him!

1291
01:22:39,080 --> 01:22:40,206
...which we can open remotely,
so open it.

1292
01:22:40,331 --> 01:22:42,123
It is not... safe!

1293
01:22:42,124 --> 01:22:43,833
We can close the aperture later

1294
01:22:43,834 --> 01:22:45,585
by inputting
the coordinates, correct?

1295
01:22:45,586 --> 01:22:47,171
- Theoretically.
- Great!

1296
01:22:48,839 --> 01:22:52,051
If we can't find him,
we'll need to draw him out.

1297
01:23:11,821 --> 01:23:13,446
But Lex,
that could tear

1298
01:23:13,447 --> 01:23:16,074
a dimensional rift
into the surrounding area!

1299
01:23:16,075 --> 01:23:18,160
This is something
you think I don't know?

1300
01:23:22,206 --> 01:23:25,418
- That shouldn't happen.
- Oh, you don't say!

1301
01:23:25,960 --> 01:23:29,797
- Can you... Can you stop it?
- Can I stop it?

1302
01:23:35,803 --> 01:23:39,974
This is why you don't create
a damn pocket universe.

1303
01:23:40,266 --> 01:23:42,893
There. Superman
won't be able to ignore that.

1304
01:23:45,187 --> 01:23:47,064
Now we know where he'll be next.

1305
01:24:29,023 --> 01:24:31,358
Thought you was out here.

1306
01:24:32,735 --> 01:24:33,611
Hey, Pa.

1307
01:24:34,612 --> 01:24:37,406
Never seen you sleep that long.

1308
01:24:41,786 --> 01:24:46,874
Last week me, Ma,
Hector and them,

1309
01:24:46,999 --> 01:24:50,294
we took a drive
to Beerki's Burritos

1310
01:24:50,419 --> 01:24:51,754
down in Luttus.

1311
01:24:52,797 --> 01:24:55,715
Like the one that used to be out
by that old, uh, blue barn,

1312
01:24:55,716 --> 01:24:57,551
out on that I-9,
you remember that?

1313
01:24:58,677 --> 01:25:02,848
- Mm-hmm.
- Burritos still just as good.

1314
01:25:07,561 --> 01:25:10,064
That Louanne,
she-- she seems nice.

1315
01:25:10,731 --> 01:25:12,983
- It's Lois.
- Hmm?

1316
01:25:13,359 --> 01:25:14,443
Her name's Lois.

1317
01:25:15,069 --> 01:25:16,779
But yeah, she's... she's nice.

1318
01:25:18,948 --> 01:25:21,158
But you don't seem
quite yourself.

1319
01:25:23,077 --> 01:25:25,787
Yeah, well, that message
that my parents sent with me,

1320
01:25:25,788 --> 01:25:27,957
I had never heard
the second half before.

1321
01:25:28,791 --> 01:25:33,211
Well, I'd say what you wanted
that message to mean

1322
01:25:33,212 --> 01:25:35,171
says a whole lot more about you

1323
01:25:35,172 --> 01:25:38,299
than what anyone meant
for it to mean.

1324
01:25:38,300 --> 01:25:39,969
Pa, you don't understand.

1325
01:25:43,472 --> 01:25:45,474
I'm not who I thought I was.

1326
01:25:50,729 --> 01:25:52,398
They sent me here
to hurt people.

1327
01:25:53,357 --> 01:25:55,400
Parents aren't for
telling their children

1328
01:25:55,401 --> 01:25:56,944
who they're supposed to be.

1329
01:25:58,487 --> 01:26:01,072
We are here to give y'aII tools,

1330
01:26:01,073 --> 01:26:03,283
help you make
fools of yourselves

1331
01:26:03,284 --> 01:26:05,953
all on your own.

1332
01:26:11,333 --> 01:26:12,167
No.

1333
01:26:14,378 --> 01:26:17,590
Your choices, Clark.

1334
01:26:18,424 --> 01:26:20,301
Your actions.

1335
01:26:22,303 --> 01:26:26,432
That's what makes you
who you are.

1336
01:26:28,225 --> 01:26:29,768
I'll tell you something, son.

1337
01:26:31,437 --> 01:26:32,855
I couldn't be...

1338
01:26:37,526 --> 01:26:39,862
...more proud of you.

1339
01:26:49,079 --> 01:26:50,414
Ol' mush.

1340
01:26:51,165 --> 01:26:53,626
Clark, there's something
on the box you might wanna see.

1341
01:26:57,212 --> 01:26:58,588
And over in Eastern Europe,

1342
01:26:58,589 --> 01:27:00,424
Boravian troops
gather at the border,

1343
01:27:00,549 --> 01:27:02,008
seemingly mere minutes away

1344
01:27:02,009 --> 01:27:04,344
from invading
Jarhanpur once again.

1345
01:27:04,345 --> 01:27:06,262
Now,
nearby villagers are willing

1346
01:27:06,263 --> 01:27:07,722
and ready
to defend their country,

1347
01:27:07,723 --> 01:27:11,434
despite the exponentially
superior firepower

1348
01:27:11,435 --> 01:27:13,394
of the well-trained Boravian military.

1349
01:27:28,452 --> 01:27:29,702
The villagers cling onto

1350
01:27:29,703 --> 01:27:31,330
what little hope they have left,

1351
01:27:31,664 --> 01:27:33,624
as they're surrounded
by the military.

1352
01:27:33,999 --> 01:27:37,001
Boravian president,
Vasil Ghurkos, says the invasion

1353
01:27:37,002 --> 01:27:38,670
is to protect
the Jarhanpurian people

1354
01:27:38,671 --> 01:27:40,130
from a tyrannical government.

1355
01:27:48,931 --> 01:28:10,119
Superman! Superman! Superman!

1356
01:28:12,496 --> 01:28:14,957
Without Superman
here to stop it this time,

1357
01:28:15,082 --> 01:28:17,876
the Jarhanpurians don't have much hope.

1358
01:28:18,419 --> 01:28:21,254
I cleaned your boots.
I'll go get 'em for you.

1359
01:28:22,798 --> 01:28:23,881
Superman.

1360
01:28:23,882 --> 01:28:25,842
We need you here in Metropolis now.

1361
01:28:25,843 --> 01:28:27,301
I have to get to Boravia, Terrific.

1362
01:28:27,302 --> 01:28:29,637
There won't be a Boravia,
or a Metropolis,

1363
01:28:29,638 --> 01:28:31,889
or a Planet Earth,
if you don't get here soon.

1364
01:28:32,808 --> 01:28:34,559
This rift is about to
tear into the city.

1365
01:28:34,560 --> 01:28:37,354
I can't stop it.
I need your help.

1366
01:28:40,107 --> 01:28:41,899
All Metropolis citizens.

1367
01:28:41,900 --> 01:28:44,610
This is a mandatory evacuation.

1368
01:28:44,611 --> 01:28:47,865
this evacuation
is not optional.

1369
01:28:49,658 --> 01:28:52,160
This is a mandatory evacuation.

1370
01:28:52,161 --> 01:28:56,081
this evacuation is not optional.

1371
01:28:58,667 --> 01:29:01,210
This is a mandatory evacuation.

1372
01:29:08,343 --> 01:29:10,303
Yeah, I'm sure
she's scared, but find her.

1373
01:29:10,304 --> 01:29:11,722
Yeah, we're all equally scared.

1374
01:29:12,473 --> 01:29:14,058
Come on, just put her on.

1375
01:29:14,767 --> 01:29:17,061
Please, Juanita, can you put
Persephone on the phone?

1376
01:29:17,770 --> 01:29:20,396
Yes, she will care! Cats
know the sound of your voice!

1377
01:29:20,397 --> 01:29:22,858
So, I was able to connect
with our contact at BodaBank.

1378
01:29:23,233 --> 01:29:24,610
Luthor's been
selling arms to Ghurkos

1379
01:29:24,735 --> 01:29:26,944
for pennies
on the dollar for years.

1380
01:29:26,945 --> 01:29:29,448
- Why, you ask?
- I do ask why.

1381
01:29:29,907 --> 01:29:33,409
He did it in exchange
for half of Jarhanpur.

1382
01:29:33,410 --> 01:29:34,327
You're kidding.

1383
01:29:34,328 --> 01:29:36,704
At first, I thought Eve
was just sending me selfies.

1384
01:29:36,705 --> 01:29:38,790
But in the background
of the shots

1385
01:29:38,791 --> 01:29:40,541
are maps, contracts,

1386
01:29:40,542 --> 01:29:43,086
all kinds of documents
chronicling Boravia's agreement

1387
01:29:43,087 --> 01:29:44,921
to cede half of the country
to Lex Luthor

1388
01:29:44,922 --> 01:29:46,714
once the invasion is complete.

1389
01:29:46,715 --> 01:29:48,175
He wants to make himself king.

1390
01:29:48,675 --> 01:29:50,385
- King?
- King.

1391
01:29:50,844 --> 01:29:52,596
Should we really
still be standing here?

1392
01:29:53,347 --> 01:29:55,473
Lois, you got that flying
saucer deal up on the roof?

1393
01:29:55,474 --> 01:29:58,309
- Yup.
- Grant. Troupe.

1394
01:29:58,310 --> 01:29:59,852
- Come on.
- Grab the board, Jimmy.

1395
01:29:59,853 --> 01:30:02,855
- How many does it hold?
- Five, or six. Six.

1396
01:30:02,856 --> 01:30:06,359
- Okay. Lombard, you too.
- Oh, thank you.

1397
01:30:06,360 --> 01:30:08,694
Why the hell would Lex
want half a desert?

1398
01:30:08,695 --> 01:30:10,404
His cultish acolytes believe
he's gonna create

1399
01:30:10,405 --> 01:30:12,448
a technologically advanced utopia.

1400
01:30:12,449 --> 01:30:13,282
Utopia?

1401
01:30:13,283 --> 01:30:14,450
There's a profit factor as well.

1402
01:30:14,451 --> 01:30:16,327
I mean,
the petroleum deposits alone

1403
01:30:16,328 --> 01:30:18,037
are worth multiples
of his investment.

1404
01:30:18,038 --> 01:30:19,373
Whatever his motives are,

1405
01:30:19,498 --> 01:30:20,790
we know Luthor
did everything he could

1406
01:30:20,791 --> 01:30:22,250
to ruin Superman's reputation.

1407
01:30:22,251 --> 01:30:23,334
Eve's photos show

1408
01:30:23,335 --> 01:30:25,753
he was behind the whole
Hammer of Boravia scam.

1409
01:30:25,754 --> 01:30:27,130
And all the bots stirring up

1410
01:30:27,131 --> 01:30:28,881
anti-Superman sentiment online.

1411
01:30:28,882 --> 01:30:31,801
Mr. Terrific believes
Luthor is also behind

1412
01:30:31,802 --> 01:30:34,303
the spreading rift
between universes out there.

1413
01:30:34,304 --> 01:30:36,305
All of it seems to be geared
toward stopping Superman

1414
01:30:36,306 --> 01:30:38,600
from standing in the way
of the Boravian invasion, Chief.

1415
01:30:39,143 --> 01:30:41,979
Call me Perry, kid. Post the story. Fast.

1416
01:30:47,818 --> 01:30:49,443
- Buckle up, kids.
- Why don't I have a seat?

1417
01:30:49,444 --> 01:30:51,405
- Jimmy, will you transcribe?
- Uh-huh.

1418
01:30:58,203 --> 01:30:59,913
Oh, God!

1419
01:31:04,376 --> 01:31:06,836
The Daily Planet has
obtained exclusive information

1420
01:31:06,837 --> 01:31:08,963
proving that billionaire
Lex Luthor is in league

1421
01:31:08,964 --> 01:31:11,299
with Boravian dictator,
Vasil Ghurkos.

1422
01:31:19,266 --> 01:31:20,808
Clark, are you close?

1423
01:31:20,809 --> 01:31:22,393
It's about to hit Metropolis,

1424
01:31:22,394 --> 01:31:23,979
and my codes
are not shutting it down.

1425
01:31:25,105 --> 01:31:26,189
Shit!

1426
01:31:43,790 --> 01:31:44,625
Uh-oh.

1427
01:31:52,382 --> 01:31:55,176
Lex! The rift is almost here!

1428
01:31:55,177 --> 01:31:56,802
So slow it down.

1429
01:31:56,803 --> 01:31:58,554
I can't unless I can
put the code in to stop it.

1430
01:31:58,555 --> 01:31:59,973
Hold on a minute then.

1431
01:32:00,682 --> 01:32:03,142
- We gotta go, man!
- Otis!

1432
01:32:23,121 --> 01:32:25,457
Not sure where we're gonna land
when the world is gone.

1433
01:33:25,684 --> 01:33:26,726
There's a code to close the rift,

1434
01:33:26,727 --> 01:33:28,437
but it's too complicated
to hack.

1435
01:33:28,729 --> 01:33:30,813
Luthor will have the code
at LuthorCorp.

1436
01:33:30,814 --> 01:33:32,816
Just give me a minute.
I'll get Krypto, and we'll go--

1437
01:33:32,941 --> 01:33:34,525
You brought that dog, man?

1438
01:33:34,526 --> 01:33:37,778
Yeah, I didn't-- didn't want him
killing my parents' cows.

1439
01:33:57,883 --> 01:33:58,674
Go on wide.

1440
01:33:58,675 --> 01:33:59,843
Wrong.
Focus on The Engineer.

1441
01:33:59,968 --> 01:34:01,762
- I'm on the alien, Larry.
- 7R.

1442
01:34:21,448 --> 01:34:22,823
It's not too late for either of you.

1443
01:34:22,824 --> 01:34:23,657
5A!

1444
01:34:23,658 --> 01:34:25,118
You don't have to do
what Luthor--

1445
01:34:48,642 --> 01:34:50,102
2X!

1446
01:34:56,066 --> 01:34:57,817
Now, Angela, as planned,

1447
01:34:57,818 --> 01:35:00,444
fill his lungs
and kill the son of a bitch.

1448
01:35:42,696 --> 01:35:45,156
Can't he hold his breath
for over an hour?

1449
01:35:45,157 --> 01:35:47,032
Not without air in his lungs.

1450
01:35:47,033 --> 01:35:48,367
He'll be dead in minutes.

1451
01:35:48,368 --> 01:35:50,035
The nanites
are suppressing his optic nerve.

1452
01:35:50,036 --> 01:35:52,330
Sight and X-ray vision
should be completely muted.

1453
01:35:52,456 --> 01:35:53,582
Lungs breached.

1454
01:35:59,546 --> 01:36:01,339
Da?

1455
01:36:04,801 --> 01:36:07,804
We will not sleep

1456
01:36:08,430 --> 01:36:11,891
until the street is flooded

1457
01:36:11,892 --> 01:36:16,563
with the blood of every Jarhanpurian!

1458
01:36:51,806 --> 01:36:53,225
What's his game?

1459
01:36:54,559 --> 01:36:56,685
Using friction
to get the nanites off?

1460
01:36:56,686 --> 01:36:58,354
Doesn't matter
if he gets them off his face.

1461
01:36:58,355 --> 01:37:00,064
The nanites
are still in his lungs.

1462
01:37:00,065 --> 01:37:01,982
Engineer, Ultraman, keep up.

1463
01:37:01,983 --> 01:37:03,692
We're trying.

1464
01:37:07,864 --> 01:37:09,782
- Maintain LOS.
- Yes. No shit, Larry.

1465
01:37:09,783 --> 01:37:10,617
Hurry.

1466
01:37:31,054 --> 01:37:32,305
He'll suffocate any minute.

1467
01:37:40,355 --> 01:37:42,314
Engineer, envelop him completely.

1468
01:38:08,967 --> 01:38:10,802
Wait! Wait, wait!
What is he doing?

1469
01:38:18,268 --> 01:38:21,730
I won't be able to sustain
the impact at this speed.

1470
01:38:23,815 --> 01:38:26,610
No, Angela, unsheathe!
He's the only one protected!

1471
01:38:43,543 --> 01:38:47,504
Entering the hole. Infrared, please?

1472
01:38:54,262 --> 01:38:55,847
Switch to night vision.

1473
01:38:59,768 --> 01:39:00,685
Whoa.

1474
01:39:28,380 --> 01:39:30,632
Her heart's still beating,
but she's unconscious.

1475
01:39:31,132 --> 01:39:32,132
Call in the Raptors.

1476
01:39:59,744 --> 01:40:01,496
What the hell?

1477
01:40:01,621 --> 01:40:05,499
That's right. Cloning you
was relatively simple.

1478
01:40:05,500 --> 01:40:08,293
All it took was combing
the aftermath of your battles...

1479
01:40:08,294 --> 01:40:10,254
...until I
located a strand of your hair.

1480
01:40:10,255 --> 01:40:13,006
That's how you got
into the Fortress.

1481
01:40:13,007 --> 01:40:14,259
You had my DNA.

1482
01:40:14,551 --> 01:40:17,469
Yes, but as is often the case
with cloning,

1483
01:40:17,470 --> 01:40:18,804
the match was imperfect.

1484
01:40:18,805 --> 01:40:23,308
He might be even stupider
than you. If that's possible.

1485
01:40:23,309 --> 01:40:24,727
But easier to control.

1486
01:40:24,728 --> 01:40:26,896
- 3L.
- And stronger.

1487
01:40:28,231 --> 01:40:29,149
22K!

1488
01:40:32,110 --> 01:40:33,111
31D!

1489
01:40:34,070 --> 01:40:34,946
2A!

1490
01:40:36,072 --> 01:40:37,615
5B! 5B!

1491
01:40:38,491 --> 01:40:40,410
6K! 9A!

1492
01:40:42,120 --> 01:40:44,664
My brain will always win!

1493
01:40:44,789 --> 01:40:47,541
Brain beats brawn!

1494
01:41:39,302 --> 01:41:44,641
Superman. Superman.

1495
01:41:50,104 --> 01:41:51,898
No matter what you do to me,
Luthor,

1496
01:41:53,066 --> 01:41:54,858
your plans in Boravia
won't work.

1497
01:41:54,859 --> 01:41:57,654
Oh, really? Why's that?

1498
01:41:58,029 --> 01:41:59,781
'Cause I called in some friends.

1499
01:42:00,365 --> 01:42:01,574
Mr. Luthor?

1500
01:42:02,909 --> 01:42:04,619
There is an anomaly
at the border.

1501
01:42:17,382 --> 01:42:18,550
Sorry, kid.

1502
01:42:19,092 --> 01:42:20,468
Superman couldn't make it.

1503
01:42:21,386 --> 01:42:22,886
So you got an upgrade.

1504
01:42:49,664 --> 01:42:52,333
Our forces aren't prepared
to deal with metahuman anomalies.

1505
01:42:52,792 --> 01:42:54,418
I've sent the word to retreat.

1506
01:42:54,419 --> 01:42:55,670
Retreat?!

1507
01:42:55,920 --> 01:42:57,504
No! No! No!

1508
01:42:57,505 --> 01:42:59,132
We must get to the bunker!

1509
01:42:59,382 --> 01:43:00,215
The bunker!

1510
01:43:17,025 --> 01:43:18,860
I know you won't kill me.

1511
01:43:19,360 --> 01:43:23,488
You are too delicate and weak,
like Superman.

1512
01:43:23,489 --> 01:43:25,825
I'm not like Superman.

1513
01:43:33,374 --> 01:43:35,668
- It's perfect. Post it, kid.
- On it.

1514
01:43:42,091 --> 01:43:43,926
I think you overestimate
the importance

1515
01:43:43,927 --> 01:43:46,470
of Jarhanpur to me,
Superman.

1516
01:43:46,471 --> 01:43:48,056
That was just a bonus.

1517
01:43:48,723 --> 01:43:50,140
I'm not killing you

1518
01:43:50,141 --> 01:43:53,811
so the Boravian military
conflict can proceed.

1519
01:43:54,312 --> 01:43:58,482
I created
the Boravian military conflict

1520
01:43:58,483 --> 01:44:02,737
so I'd have an excuse
to kill you!

1521
01:44:03,112 --> 01:44:04,863
Once you involved yourself,

1522
01:44:04,864 --> 01:44:06,323
I knew I could easily get

1523
01:44:06,324 --> 01:44:08,368
